# The server stage needs the package, its sources and tests (SwiftPM checks every target's path) and
# the submodule's source folders; the client stage needs web/, with web/e2e because Vite reads
# every project tsconfig.json names; the runtime needs LICENSE. Everything else stays out, so edits
# to docs, scripts, the Mac-only tools or CI do not invalidate a build layer.
.build
.swiftpm
.claude
**/.git
**/.DS_Store
**/node_modules
.env
tei
docs
fixtures
scripts
tools
.github
README.md
CLAUDE.md
compose.yaml
upstream/FRUS-Explorer/Planning
upstream/FRUS-Explorer/Docs
upstream/FRUS-Explorer/Vendor
web/dist
web/test-results
web/playwright-report
